body:grpc {
  name: message 1
  content: '''
    {
      "owner_address": "QeVS9kh1hcK1i8LJu0SSvB8XEyzQ",
      "contract_address": "QaYU+AO2/XgJhqQseOycf3fm3tE8",
      "data": "cKCCMQAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOVS9kh1hcK1i8LJu0SSvB8XEyzQ",
      "call_value": 0
    }
  '''
}

docs {
  Builds an **unsigned** transaction that executes a state-changing smart-contract
  call (`TransactionExtention`). Sign it locally and submit via
  `BroadcastTransaction`.

  - `data`: base64 of the ABI-encoded function call.
  - `call_value`: TRX (in SUN) to send with the call.

  **Service:** `protocol.Wallet` · **Method:** `TriggerContract` (unary)

  All `bytes` fields are sent as **base64 of the raw bytes** (protobuf JSON mapping).
  For a TRON address, base58-decode it (or take the 21-byte hex form starting with `41`)
  and base64-encode the raw bytes, e.g. `echo 41E552...32CD0 | xxd -r -p | base64`.
}
